  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In March 2026 testimony, Amanda Parkhill stated that NCUA is using AI for content generation, flagging anomalies in Call Report data submissions, forecasting loan performance, identifying elevated-risk credit unions, and enhancing cybersecurity operations. She also said NCUA is evaluating opportunities through GSA's USAi shared services and that the agency added an AI Resources page in August 2025 covering use cases, implementation, risk management, data security, and cybersecurity risks. Parkhill described the page as providing AI-specific risk management resources to help credit unions make informed decisions when implementing AI or partnering with AI service providers.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s7",
    "s8",
    "s2"
   ],
